WEBVTT

00:01.000 --> 00:04.546
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.630 --> 00:08.092
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.092 --> 00:11.846
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:11.930 --> 00:14.014
"On which we used to rely?

00:14.765 --> 00:17.977
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.103 --> 00:23.108
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.191 --> 00:24.652
"Laugh and cry

00:24.777 --> 00:30.198
"He's a family guy

00:38.334 --> 00:41.962
That's funny. I don't remember
buying Stewie these toys.

00:45.423 --> 00:49.261
My God. It all makes sense now.

00:49.386 --> 00:54.184
My baby is some kind of diabolical genius
bent on world domination!

00:56.895 --> 01:00.732
Bravo, Lois. The last horse
finally crosses the finish line.

01:00.857 --> 01:05.029
All these months I should've been paying
attention to what you've been saying.

01:05.112 --> 01:06.781
You're an evil child.

01:06.906 --> 01:10.535
Why? Why did I have to go and smoke pot
when I was pregnant with you?

01:10.660 --> 01:15.456
Cheer up. Be proud. You've given birth
to the future emperor of the world.

01:15.456 --> 01:19.003
Pity you won't be around
to enjoy it. Cheerio.

01:19.086 --> 01:21.380
Aaagh!

01:21.505 --> 01:23.466
- Lois! Lois!
- Huh? Hm?

01:23.592 --> 01:26.803
- What's the matter?
- I just had the strangest dream.

01:26.928 --> 01:31.516
Something about Stewie
and Cheerios... It's gone.

01:31.516 --> 01:34.228
Come on, get up.
It's opening day for the Sox.

01:34.311 --> 01:36.731
Hey, Chris, Meg! We're going to Fenway!

01:36.815 --> 01:39.859
You can't pull the kids out of school
for a baseball game.

01:39.942 --> 01:43.196
Nothing they learn in school
they can't learn on the street.

01:43.280 --> 01:46.533
- It's 3 o'clock. Where the hell is Louie?
- You tell me.

01:46.617 --> 01:50.580
Louie left his house at 2.15
and has to travel a distance of 6.2 miles

01:50.705 --> 01:54.249
at a rate of five miles per hour.
What time will Louie arrive?

01:54.333 --> 01:57.796
- Depends if he stops to see his ho.
- That's called a variable.

01:57.879 --> 02:01.340
- Look what I made for the game.
- What's that mean anyway?

02:01.424 --> 02:06.221
- "And the Lord said 'Go, Sox. "'
- Dad, don't you have to work today?

02:06.346 --> 02:10.184
It's nothing a little phone call
can't take care of.

02:11.226 --> 02:14.480
- Hello?
- Mr Weed? I can't come to work today.

02:14.563 --> 02:19.695
I was in a terrible plane crash. My entire
family was killed and I am a vegetable.

02:19.778 --> 02:22.281
I'll see you tomorrow.
Huh? Huh?

02:22.406 --> 02:25.743
Please, Peter. Your excuses
are lamer than FDR's legs.

02:27.411 --> 02:28.454
Too soon?

02:32.834 --> 02:36.672
- Here it comes, Jeremy!
- I got it! I got it!

02:36.797 --> 02:41.803
Yes! Yeah! Whoo! All right!
I'm the man! Yeah!

02:41.887 --> 02:46.474
Hold on to this. It'll be a souvenir of your
first Major League game with your Dad.

02:46.598 --> 02:49.395
My God! I shall cherish this for ever.

02:49.520 --> 02:52.439
I'll trade you this baseball
for your souvenir bat.

02:52.522 --> 02:55.359
- Sure.
- What did you learn?

02:55.359 --> 02:59.531
We haven't done anything together like this
since we saw Mike Tyson get beat.

02:59.614 --> 03:03.785
All right, Mike.
The word again is "onomatopoeia".

03:03.910 --> 03:07.538
- Uh, C.
- I'm sorry. That's incorrect.

03:07.663 --> 03:08.791
Oh, dang.

03:08.916 --> 03:12.545
I'm so glad you talked us all
into playing hooky.

03:12.670 --> 03:16.632
Me, too. Maybe we can get on TV if we take
our shirts off and run onto the field.

03:16.715 --> 03:20.177
- I'm not taking my shirt off.
- There. Now they're old news.

03:20.261 --> 03:23.097
- Peter!
- Go, Sox! Go...

03:23.181 --> 03:25.058
Aaargh!

03:29.022 --> 03:31.107
Hm.

03:34.862 --> 03:38.532
- Peter?
- Oh... Hi, Mr Weed.

03:38.615 --> 03:42.494
- It seems you've made a full recovery.
- Oh, yeah. Yeah.

03:42.578 --> 03:45.830
That plane crash I told you about,
it turned out to be gas.

03:45.913 --> 03:49.460
Aha! Liar. Tomorrow, my office, 9.30.

03:49.585 --> 03:53.339
I'm tired of Mr Weed treating me
like a common doormat.

03:53.339 --> 03:57.720
I want him to treat me like a deluxe one
from Pottery Barn with the fancy straw.

03:57.720 --> 03:59.887
I don't care for Pottery Barn.

04:00.013 --> 04:03.642
If you want Mr Weed to respect you,
you're gonna have to earn it.

04:03.768 --> 04:06.980
Earn it...

04:09.190 --> 04:13.361
- Why have you forsaken me?
- Mr Weed?

04:13.361 --> 04:17.617
I heard you ran into my identical twin
brother at the ball game yesterday.

04:17.742 --> 04:20.453
If you don't buy that,
sorry I was at the ball game.

04:20.453 --> 04:23.247
Peter, I just received terrible news.

04:23.372 --> 04:26.375
This company has been taken over
by a conglomerate.

04:26.501 --> 04:30.129
After 23 years of faithful service,
I've been terminated!

04:30.256 --> 04:32.841
Wow. The business world sure is funny.

04:33.592 --> 04:38.597
What do you call it when a guy in middle
management moves to upper management?

04:38.680 --> 04:41.810
- I don't know. What do you call it?
- A promotion.

04:41.935 --> 04:45.772
Oh, thanks. Here's a memo.

04:49.860 --> 04:51.945
Sometimes the business world's funny.

04:56.117 --> 04:59.245
And so on behalf of
the El Dorado Cigarette Company,

04:59.330 --> 05:02.457
I'd like to welcome you to our family.

05:02.582 --> 05:07.172
I think you'll be very happy
with the changes we've made.

05:07.172 --> 05:10.799
This is sweet! Why are you
putting a window in the factory?

05:10.924 --> 05:13.303
So Aunt Bee has a place
to let her pies cool.

05:13.428 --> 05:18.015
Hello, boys. Today's pie is cherry.
It'll be ready just in time for lunch.

05:18.098 --> 05:21.645
Wow. These guys sure know
how to run a company.

05:21.770 --> 05:24.063
Look how happy those morons are.

05:24.147 --> 05:27.693
They'll never realise we're using toys
to get children addicted

05:27.818 --> 05:29.988
to our company's cigarettes.

05:32.616 --> 05:36.245
Good boy, Connor.

05:36.370 --> 05:38.663
Pull.

05:47.715 --> 05:52.305
Can't we eat? I'm so hungry,
I could ride a horse.

05:52.430 --> 05:56.267
I don't get it.
I could ride it to the store, I guess.

05:56.392 --> 06:01.397
I told you we're not starting without your
father. Dinner just isn't dinner without him.

06:01.481 --> 06:06.611
Perhaps I could help simulate the
experience. Yum, yum, yum...

06:09.114 --> 06:14.328
Hey, family, anyone in the mood for lobster?
Ow! Oh, God! One of them has my pupil!

06:14.411 --> 06:15.788
Agh, agh, agh!

06:15.871 --> 06:17.665
Oh, God! Agh! Agh!

06:17.748 --> 06:19.209
Ah.

06:19.334 --> 06:21.711
How can you afford lobster on your salary?

06:21.836 --> 06:24.213
- I got a raise.
- What?!

06:24.339 --> 06:26.425
The new owners gave everyone raises.

06:26.425 --> 06:29.552
Even Kenneth, the badass mail clerk
with the heart of gold.

06:30.387 --> 06:34.225
- Hi, Kenneth. Did I get any mail?
- No! If you come any closer, I'll slice ya!

06:34.350 --> 06:36.936
OK, OK. Man, what a badass.

06:37.061 --> 06:40.482
Yeah? That "badass" just gave
half his pay cheque to orphans.

06:40.607 --> 06:42.692
Orphans with diseases.

06:48.199 --> 06:50.701
And check out the new toys we're making.

06:50.827 --> 06:52.495
Baby Smokes-A-Lot?

06:53.538 --> 06:56.332
Tastes like happy.

06:56.457 --> 06:58.544
Cool! That's imitatable.

06:58.627 --> 07:02.798
What the hell? "El Dorado Cigarettes"?
That's who bought your company?

07:02.923 --> 07:05.635
Oh, my God!
They're trying to corrupt our children!

07:05.718 --> 07:09.472
Those bastards turned a whole generation
of Americans into smokers

07:09.597 --> 07:11.684
with subliminal advertising.

07:11.684 --> 07:14.895
- Timmy, where's Lassie?
- She's out in the orchard, Ma.

07:15.020 --> 07:17.731
Peaches are coming
in mighty early this year.

07:17.731 --> 07:18.650
Smoke.

07:18.774 --> 07:22.194
You know what they say:
"Early peaches, long summer".

07:22.319 --> 07:23.154
Smoke.

07:23.780 --> 07:25.949
What's that, Lassie?

07:26.074 --> 07:27.325
Are ya smoking yet?

07:27.409 --> 07:31.080
If kids see this doll,
they're gonna think smoking's OK.

07:31.080 --> 07:34.082
You have to talk to these
new bosses in the morning.

07:34.207 --> 07:37.962
Don't worry, Lois. I'll set 'em straight.
Just like I did with Chris.

07:39.213 --> 07:43.469
- Dad, what's the blowhole for?
- I'll tell you what it's not for, son.

07:43.594 --> 07:47.764
And when I do, you'll understand
why I can never go back to SeaWorld.

07:50.977 --> 07:54.855
We need to talk. My wife says
you're trying to get kids to smoke.

07:54.855 --> 07:57.776
- That's just not true.
- What about this toy?

07:57.859 --> 07:59.945
It's just a doll with a cigarette.

08:00.070 --> 08:05.283
Barbie has a Dream Car, but you don't see
eight-year-old kids driving. They're fun toys.

08:05.367 --> 08:07.453
- Smoke.
- Not now, Jerry.

08:07.578 --> 08:11.540
Trust me. The last thing we want
is to get kids to start smoking.

08:11.624 --> 08:14.127
What about that graph on the wall that says

08:14.252 --> 08:17.173
"The first thing we want
is to get kids to start smoking. "

08:17.256 --> 08:20.175
That's just something
my son made me in art class.

08:20.300 --> 08:23.012
Huh. Then what about that poster that says

08:23.095 --> 08:27.183
"The graph was not made in art class.
We really do want kids to start smoking. "

08:27.267 --> 08:29.059
We're a caring company.

08:29.144 --> 08:34.273
I mean, would you really be the president
of a company that didn't care about kids?

08:34.357 --> 08:39.154
- No. But I'm not the president.
- Yes, you are... if you want to be.

08:39.279 --> 08:40.406
Ah.

08:40.531 --> 08:43.951
Oh, wow. Imagine me, president.

08:51.042 --> 08:52.628
I'll do it!

08:56.173 --> 08:58.259
- How did it go?
- I'm not finished yet.

09:03.890 --> 09:07.644
- Aren't you gonna ask me how it went?
- Did you talk to the executives?

09:07.727 --> 09:10.147
Peter, answer me!

09:10.147 --> 09:13.275
- I did. They made me president.
- Of the whole company?

09:13.359 --> 09:14.818
All right, Dad!

09:14.943 --> 09:19.116
You shoulda seen the way they treated me.
I've never gotten that respect before.

09:20.241 --> 09:23.079
- Great work-out, Bobby.
- Up yours, sack-breath!

09:23.162 --> 09:24.955
That's Mr Griffin.

09:24.955 --> 09:27.457
Peter, why would they make you president?

09:27.540 --> 09:32.671
Maybe it's because I can recite all
50 states in a quarter of a second.

09:32.755 --> 09:37.468
- That was just a loud yelping noise.
- Jeez, Lois. I thought you'd be proud of me.

09:37.468 --> 09:40.680
The company finally thinks
I'm worth something.

09:40.805 --> 09:42.975
Wait till you see all the perks we get.

09:46.311 --> 09:49.148
Um... hi. Can I help you?

09:49.148 --> 09:53.194
Some company hired me to stand next
to you all day, so you'd look better.

09:53.319 --> 09:56.114
- That's ridiculous.
- Meg? Did you get less ugly?

09:56.239 --> 09:57.282
Yeah!

09:59.659 --> 10:03.122
- Surprise!
- Everything looks the same.

10:03.206 --> 10:04.457
It looks the same.

10:04.582 --> 10:09.462
But El Dorado Cigarettes coated the inside
of the house with a microfilm of Teflon,

10:09.587 --> 10:10.630
so it's easy to clean.

10:10.714 --> 10:11.966
Oh.

10:13.132 --> 10:15.511
Maybe I shouldn't have had 'em do the floors.

10:15.636 --> 10:17.388
I'm Nudes on Ice!

10:18.556 --> 10:22.935
This is so exciting.
Your father's first day as president.

10:22.935 --> 10:24.896
Good morning, First Family.

10:26.355 --> 10:29.484
- Lois, what's in this coffee?
- Isn't it wonderful?

10:29.610 --> 10:32.737
They sent Martha Stewart
to help me with the housework.

10:32.820 --> 10:37.535
I take back all the bad things I said
about them. The coffee is delicious, Martha.

10:37.618 --> 10:42.832
A little chicory perks up the taste
of roasted coffee beans. It's a good thing.

10:42.957 --> 10:49.006
I think it's a crappy thing!
In fact, this is my last cigarette ever.

10:50.049 --> 10:53.469
You make me sick being bought off
with a few lousy perks.

10:53.595 --> 10:56.181
Oh, I beg to differ.

10:59.433 --> 11:04.439
Oh, you don't need to park here, Mr Griffin.
You have an executive parking space now.

11:04.523 --> 11:06.526
That looks exactly like my old space.

11:06.609 --> 11:09.320
This one comes
with your own company suck-up.

11:09.445 --> 11:11.738
- Morning. Nice day.
- It's a little cloudy.

11:11.822 --> 11:15.076
Absolutely. One of the worst days
I've seen in years.

11:15.076 --> 11:17.370
- Good news about the Yankees.
- I hate them.

11:17.453 --> 11:20.166
Pack of cheaters, they are. I love your tie.

11:20.291 --> 11:23.627
- I hate this tie.
- It's awful, it's gaudy, it's gotta go.

11:23.627 --> 11:27.800
- And I hate myself.
- You make me sick, you fat sack of crap.

11:27.882 --> 11:30.093
- I'm the president
- The best there is.

11:30.177 --> 11:33.931
- But you just said you hated me.
- But... not you the president.

11:34.056 --> 11:39.562
The you who said you hated you.
You, who love, hate, Yankees, clouds...

11:41.021 --> 11:43.232
I'll have that fixed for you, sir.

11:44.691 --> 11:49.781
Here's your new digs. Now get
to work, sport. We're counting on you.

11:52.701 --> 11:58.248
Wow. My own office.
I guess I'd better get busy.

12:12.223 --> 12:14.308
Agh!

12:26.197 --> 12:28.365
Gentlemen, we have a problem.

12:28.491 --> 12:32.037
There's an anti-smoking bill
that could put us out of business.

12:32.120 --> 12:35.791
Yes. Apparently, causing cancer
is this year's "hot button".

12:35.791 --> 12:39.211
We've tried everything
to get through to these politicians.

12:39.336 --> 12:42.464
Harvard lawyers, lobbyists,
wisecracking leprechauns.

12:42.548 --> 12:46.927
Excuse me. Do you have a dollar?
I'm a little short.

12:47.053 --> 12:49.847
That's the problem.
They're idiots in Washington.

12:49.972 --> 12:53.518
Instead of a smart guy, we should
send a moron they can relate to.

12:54.978 --> 12:58.107
Where are we going to find someone
who's that stupid?

12:58.107 --> 13:02.487
- Yeah. And not just stupid. Fat, too.
- That's exactly what we need.

13:02.570 --> 13:05.823
Wait. Didn't we just make
a fat, stupid guy president?

13:05.908 --> 13:11.663
You bet we did. Gentlemen,
our new tobacco lobbyist is... that guy!

14:05.264 --> 14:09.101
So what's this big assignment
you got for me, chairman of the broad?

14:09.226 --> 14:13.814
"Chairman of the broad".
When did you become such a stitch?

14:13.898 --> 14:16.400
Don't you remember? You gave me writers.

14:16.526 --> 14:19.946
"I don't want to say you're rich,
but when you walk into a bank,

14:20.071 --> 14:23.618
all the tellers go 'Whoopee!"'

14:23.701 --> 14:26.412
That wasn't funny.
I thought you were Jewish.

14:26.537 --> 14:29.665
- He's only half-Jewish.
- You're fired.

14:29.748 --> 14:34.463
Here's the thing. Some troublemakers
in Congress are trying to shut us down.

14:34.463 --> 14:37.800
We need someone important like you
to go down to Washington

14:37.800 --> 14:40.928
and help those bastards see
what fun-loving people

14:40.928 --> 14:43.015
the tobacco industry's made of.

14:43.015 --> 14:45.099
Washington? Sweet.

14:45.182 --> 14:48.311
But I gotta warn you,
I've made some enemies on the Hill.

14:49.354 --> 14:52.899
And that's when Clarence Thomas
forced me into his chambers

14:53.024 --> 14:56.029
and showed me lewd pictures.

14:56.154 --> 14:59.699
We have indisputable evidence
that not only have you never been

14:59.782 --> 15:03.662
in the same room as Clarence Thomas,
you've never been in the same state.

15:03.662 --> 15:05.747
How do you respond to that?

15:06.790 --> 15:10.211
Bababooie! Bababooie!
Howard Stern's penis! Bababooie!

15:12.088 --> 15:14.172
How long is Dad gonna be in Washington?

15:14.297 --> 15:17.843
As long as it takes.
He's a very important man now.

15:17.843 --> 15:20.430
He's the spokesman for his entire industry.

15:32.527 --> 15:35.780
Thank you, Martha.
Brian, could you pass me the TV guide?

15:35.780 --> 15:37.324
- Piss off!
- What?

15:37.449 --> 15:40.994
I'm sorry. It just feels like for ever
since I've had a smoke.

15:41.077 --> 15:44.331
I'm just a bit testy. Stop staring at my tail!

15:46.417 --> 15:50.796
Mr Harrison? I see those government guys
you were telling me about.

15:50.880 --> 15:54.758
I'll show 'em a good time
and get 'em to come around to our side.

15:54.842 --> 15:58.596
Excuse me. Al Gore? George W Bush?

15:58.723 --> 15:59.640
- Yes?
- Yes?

15:59.765 --> 16:02.351
Great. And what's your friend's name?

16:02.477 --> 16:04.853
Dick Armey.

16:11.027 --> 16:14.865
- Oh, God. No, seriously. What's his name?
- Dick Armey.

16:23.832 --> 16:26.461
Oh. Oh, I just got it.

16:26.544 --> 16:32.592
Hey. Hey, Armey. Hey, what's your
wife's name? Vagina Coastguard?

16:32.718 --> 16:35.847
I'm kidding. Get in the car.
We're going to a skin bar.

16:35.930 --> 16:36.973
- OK.
- Great.

16:37.098 --> 16:39.391
That sounds good.

16:41.478 --> 16:45.857
Oh, my God. Oh, my God. Oh, my God.
Oh, my God. I don't know what happened.

16:45.857 --> 16:49.486
Oh, it's OK. It's OK, Senator.
This girl didn't have a family.

16:49.611 --> 16:52.948
It'll be like she never existed.
Grab ahold of yourself.

16:53.032 --> 16:58.455
You may have killed her when you shoved
all those dollar bills down her throat.

16:58.580 --> 17:02.960
You may have killed her when you hit her
with the stool. I'm not a doctor.

17:03.043 --> 17:06.713
But I'll tell you what didn't
kill her... Smoking.

17:06.797 --> 17:08.383
You have our support.

17:10.467 --> 17:14.515
Look, kids. Here's your father
in People magazine with Jim Carrey,

17:14.640 --> 17:17.642
and they're both "Sssmokin'!"

17:17.767 --> 17:21.105
I loved that in Mask. "Sssmokin'!"

17:21.189 --> 17:25.693
"Sssmokin'!" "Sssmokin'!"

17:25.693 --> 17:28.405
Do I have to listen
to this drivel 24 hours a day?!

17:28.488 --> 17:32.575
But, hey, I guess anything's better
than looking at your smelly face!

17:32.658 --> 17:35.078
- Mom!
- Honey, your face smells fine.

17:35.161 --> 17:37.790
He doesn't mean it. It's the lack of nicotine.

17:37.873 --> 17:41.543
Mom, the school janitor said
that Dad's working for the bad guys.

17:41.627 --> 17:45.505
- He said it through a hole in his throat.
- That doesn't make him right.

17:45.589 --> 17:49.052
If I had a hole in my throat,
I'd put pennies in it!

17:49.135 --> 17:52.597
Your father's doing great work.
Life's never been better.

17:52.680 --> 17:56.227
Yes. I, too, applaud the oaf
for finally showing initiative.

17:56.352 --> 17:59.981
God knows it was years overdue.

18:00.107 --> 18:03.109
You know who I saw at the market today?

18:03.234 --> 18:07.906
Patty Croft. Oh, and she has gotten fat!

18:08.031 --> 18:11.785
Oh, my God! Stewie, no!
Oh, God. What have I done?

18:11.868 --> 18:15.206
I knew smoking was bad.
But I still sold my soul.

18:15.331 --> 18:17.501
And for what? Martha Stewart?

18:17.625 --> 18:21.463
Come on, kids.
We gotta put a stop to this. Now!

18:23.048 --> 18:25.008
Finally.

18:27.428 --> 18:29.096
Ah.

18:30.764 --> 18:32.518
"They call me Bill

18:32.643 --> 18:34.935
"Yes, they call me Bill

18:35.020 --> 18:38.064
"And I'm standing here on Capitol...

18:38.064 --> 18:40.025
Aoow!

18:43.487 --> 18:47.867
Bob Dole's a friend of the tobacco industry.
Bob Dole likes your style.

18:47.950 --> 18:59.005
Bob Dole. Bob Dole. Bob Dole. Bob Dole.

18:59.130 --> 19:03.301
There you are. I caught Stewie smoking.
That cigarette company is evil.

19:03.384 --> 19:07.263
- We can't be a part of this any more.
- This is the best job I ever had!

19:07.346 --> 19:11.727
Since I became president, profits
have been higher than Alyssa Milano.

19:13.520 --> 19:17.900
- What kind of cheap shot... Joel!
- I'm suing. I'm suing. I'm on it. I'm on it.

19:17.983 --> 19:21.320
- Mr Griffin, time for your speech.
- What about your son?

19:21.445 --> 19:24.782
So Stewie had a puff.
He's old enough to make his own decisions.

19:24.866 --> 19:27.995
For God's sakes, Lois, he's one.
Cut the umbilical cord.

19:29.996 --> 19:34.794
Ladies and gentlemen of Congress, I am
here today to talk to you about smoking.

19:34.794 --> 19:37.587
Oh, please, Peter, do the right thing.

19:37.713 --> 19:41.759
I know a lot of you are already on my side.

19:41.885 --> 19:45.932
And for you naysayers,
I have two strong words for you...

19:46.057 --> 19:49.601
Come on! Come on!

19:50.643 --> 19:53.856
- OK. OK, sure.
- All right. Why not?

19:53.981 --> 19:57.318
Thank you, ladies and...

19:57.401 --> 19:59.821
...and...

20:02.532 --> 20:05.536
Baby needs to suck ash!
Baby needs to suck ash!

20:05.661 --> 20:08.456
Not "ass", you pervert.
Save it for the interns.

20:08.581 --> 20:10.959
Is that a baby?

20:11.084 --> 20:16.589
Oh, my God. That's Stewie. Lois was right.
Children under four shouldn't smoke.

20:16.714 --> 20:19.718
I don't care about this job any more.
Cigarettes are bad!

20:19.843 --> 20:23.263
Mr Griffin is right!
Smoking is a horrible vice!

20:23.388 --> 20:26.392
It shortens life expectancy
and pollutes our air.

20:26.517 --> 20:28.811
According to recent polls, air is good.

20:28.894 --> 20:32.566
Cigarettes killed my father
and raped my mother!

20:33.399 --> 20:36.528
I propose we send a message
to tobacco companies

20:36.611 --> 20:40.783
by fining the El Dorado Cigarette Company
infinity billion dollars!

20:40.908 --> 20:44.872
That's the spirit, Frank. But I think
a real number might be more effective.

20:44.955 --> 20:49.667
All in favour of fining this evil tobacco
giant $100 million dollars say "Aye".

20:49.750 --> 20:52.253
- Aye!
- But that'll bankrupt us!

20:53.421 --> 20:56.759
You mean the way you've
morally bankrupted America?

20:58.427 --> 21:01.555
Thanks for that zinger.
Give me a snappy line to go out on.

21:01.555 --> 21:04.685
Actually, our lunch is here.

21:04.768 --> 21:06.562
Uh...

21:06.645 --> 21:10.525
Well, that's my mama!

21:33.549 --> 21:37.096
Hi, I'm Peter Griffin.
We've had a lot of laughs tonight.

21:37.221 --> 21:42.308
But I'll tell you what's not funny.
Killing strippers. Strippers are people, too.

21:42.433 --> 21:47.647
Naked people who may be willing
to pleasure you for a price you negotiate.

21:47.731 --> 21:52.237
Besides, there's no need to kill 'em.
Most of them are already dead inside.

21:52.320 --> 21:54.947
Good night, everyone.

21:54.948 --> 22:55.948
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru